spans.s:
√dih (dégdhi; didihé; digdhá; -díhya).
 —1. stroke, touch lightly;
 —2. smear;
 —3. besmear, pollute. [for *dhigh: cf.
ἔθιγον, ‘touched’; Lat. fingo, ‘form, fashion,
 esp. with the hand in soft material’;
Goth. daigs, ‘moulded mass of clay or
bread-paste’; Old Eng. dāg, Eng. dough.]
+ sam, pass. (be plastered together, be
indistinct, and so) be uncertain, doubtful.
